  *
  * Writes are refused unless boot-arg sdrw=1. Every write is checked
  * against the partition bounds again right before it is issued.
+ *
+ * Persistent console log (boot-arg sdlog=1): every few seconds the console
+ * ring of bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c (all kernel printf and /dev/console output)
+ * is written to a GPT partition of its own, named "ioslog" (sdlogpart=), in
+ * the SWEETLOG format of tools/sweet-log.py: a header at offset 0, the 4 MiB
+ * ring at offset 4096. Read it on a PC with dd of that partition. It never
+ * writes outside that partition, and works with any root (also rd=md0).
  */
